From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] wordcraft-web: the host bridge lists and runs commands and
 reports a focus-out key

Phase 6 WP11 (docs/phase6/a11y-palette.md). A canvas editor has no DOM, so a screen reader sees none of its commands. In host mode the editor now answers `wordcraft:commands` with the commands that take no parameters (id, label in the editor's language, enabled, shortcut), runs `wordcraft:run { id }` through `WordApp::run` (the path of a ribbon button) and answers `wordcraft:ran { id, ok, error }`, and focuses the canvas on `wordcraft:focus`. A capture-phase keydown listener posts `wordcraft:focusOut { palette }` for F6 (leave the editor: a canvas swallows Tab, WCAG 2.1.2) and F1 (open the host's command palette); neither key is bound in the editor. The host page (the shell, the docserver wrapper) builds the accessible palette from the list. Web-sys gains the `KeyboardEvent` feature (already enabled by eframe in the build). Desktop apps and the page without `?host=parent` are unchanged.
---
 apps/wordcraft-web/Cargo.toml      |  2 +-
 apps/wordcraft-web/src/web/host.rs | 59 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 60 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

